GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:7:No source is edited, no `device_add` of our own, no boot.
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:8:
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:9:WHAT THIS IS AND IS NOT.  The pre-fix WITNESS (`_scratchpad/sh4pcic_witness.py`)
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:10:asserted the SYMPTOM -- a MEASURED census of all 137 word offsets in both
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:11:directions found 116 killing the host on a plain 32-bit READ and 125 on a write
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:12:-- so it goes red once the defect is gone, which is what a witness should do.
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:13:This file is the DETECTOR: it asserts the FIXED behaviour, fails on the pre-fix
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:14:build, and is built to fail on the mutants listed at the foot of this docstring.
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:15:Grading one by the other's clauses is a category error in either direction.
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:16:
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:17:*** THE ROW THAT MATTERS MOST IS P3, NOT P1. ***  Deleting `exit(1)` and nothing
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:18:else does not fix this defect -- it makes it worse.  The store into `pcic_reg[]`
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:19:at dev_sh4.c:875-879 is UPSTREAM of every guard, so a rejected value has ALREADY
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:20:landed by the time the guard runs, and `exit(1)` was the only thing that stopped
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:21:a guest reading it back.  P3 writes an accepted value, then a rejected one, then
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:22:READS THE REGISTER BACK through the guest; the naive fix turns a host kill into
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:23:silent state corruption, and P3 is the only row in this file that sees it.
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:24:[#556, 2026-10-02 -- a records correction; the text above is kept as it was written] silent state corruption, seen
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:25:by P3, P16, and P17.  (hsh4pcicprobe:F6: regress/artifacts/astraretro_harness_20260926/HARNESS_DISPOSITIONS.md)
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:26:
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:27:P3b is its sibling and covers the `default:` arm, whose restore is otherwise
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:28:UNOBSERVABLE: nothing else in the tree reads `pcic_reg[]`, and a `default:` read
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:29:answers 0 regardless.  It becomes observable through ADDRESS ALIASING -- the
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:30:switch dispatches on the FULL address, but PCIC_REG() indexes on the WORD, so
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:31:0xfe200015 (a byte inside PCICONF5) reaches `default:` while sharing PCICONF5's
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:32:array slot.  A byte store there clobbers the whole word on the way in; only the
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:33:restore puts it back.
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:34:
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:35:P2b uses the same aliasing in the other direction, and it is what gives "reads
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:36:answer 0" any teeth at all: on a fresh device every unimplemented slot already
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:37:holds 0, and writes to unimplemented offsets are dropped, so `odata = 0` and
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:38:`odata = pcic_reg[i]` agree EVERYWHERE until a labelled register has put a
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:39:non-zero word into a slot that `default:` can reach.
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:40:
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:41:*** SEVEN MUTANTS PASSED THE FIRST 29 ROWS.  P14-P20 ARE WHAT CLOSES THEM. ***
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:42:The 29-row file measured ONE access width, observed TWO of the ten `pcic_old`
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:43:restores, never offered any arm a SECOND rejected write, and never wrote
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:44:PCICONF0 before reading it.  Each of those blanks was a family of survivors,
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:45:not a single mutant:
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:46:
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:47:  P14/P15  the WIDTH AXIS.  `if (len == 2) exit(1);` -- the original host kill
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:48:           narrowed to one width -- passed 29/29, because len=2 was issued
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:49:           NOWHERE in the file and len=1 at only two fixed addresses.
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:50:  P16      one read-back per RESTORE.  Deleting a single restore (PCIMBR's,
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:51:           say) passed 29/29 and let a guest read its own rejected word back.
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:52:  P17/P18  the SECOND OFFENCE.  Bracing the restore INSIDE the latch -- a
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:53:           brace slip, the shape a tidy-up produces -- restores the first
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:54:           offence and silently corrupts every one after it.  29/29, ten arms.
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:55:  P19      the MUTUALLY-MASKING PAIR in the PCICONF0 arm.  Each of the two
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:56:           statements is void alone, so single-line mutation is blind to both;
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:57:           delete both and the guest gets its own word back.
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:58:  P20      the latch keyed on (offset, FAULT CLASS).  A per-offset latch merges
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:59:           two different faults that share one array slot and drops the second
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:60:           diagnostic entirely.
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:61:
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:62:P4 counts the LATCHED SUFFIX, never a register name.  Under a cold debugger
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:63:`single_step` is true, so `debug()`'s quiet_mode early-out never fires and a
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:64:probe run this way CANNOT distinguish `fatal()` from `debug()` by presence -- a
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:65:#441 detector row was passed by a two-character mutant for exactly that reason.
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:66:P5 is P4's other half: a PER-DEVICE latch passes P4 and fails P5.
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:67:
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:68:NO SH-4 MANUAL IS CITED ANYWHERE IN THIS FILE, and every constant below is read
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:69:out of a header in this repository -- with the file and line named -- or measured.
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:70:
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:71:*** THE REASON GIVEN FOR THAT CHANGED ON 2026-08-22, AND THE PRACTICE DID NOT. ***
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:72:This paragraph used to say there was no SH-4 manual in the tree, which was true
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:73:when it was written (`_scratchpad/sh4_manual.txt` is one byte) and is FALSE now:
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:74:a real SH7750 Hardware Manual (Rev.7.00, REJ09B0366-0700) and SH-4 Software
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:75:Manual were obtained by owner directive and extracted to
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:76:`_scratchpad/sh7750_hardware.txt` and `_scratchpad/sh4_programming.txt`.
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:77:
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:78:The file still cites none, deliberately.  A probe's constants should come from
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:79:the headers the CODE actually compiles against, because a probe that agrees with
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:80:the manual while the code disagrees with both would be green and useless.  The
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:81:manual is now available for deciding what the code OUGHT to do; the headers
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:82:remain the authority on what it DOES.
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:83:
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:84:usage:  sh4_pcic_probe.py <gxemul-binary> <landisk-kernel> [--jobs N] [--fast]
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:85:
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:86:    *** KEEP THE "./" ON THE BINARY. ***  `os.execvp` on a bare name searches
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:87:    PATH; when it misses, EVERY arm silently reports alive=False and a probe
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:88:    written the naive way "passes" having measured nothing.  P0 catches that,
GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh4_pcic_probe.py:89:    and the existence check in main() catches it sooner.
