1:#!/usr/bin/env python3
2:"""armmsrmodekill -- RUNG-3 WITNESS.  One privileged MSR ends the PROCESS on `-E testarm'.
3:
4:BUILT FROM regress/artifacts/armmsrmodekill/WITNESSSPEC_REWRITE_grok_20260917.txt, which is a
5:REWRITE and not the original 16-row spec plus eight sticky notes.  That spec's amendments file
6:carries a SUPERSEDED banner; do not build from it.
7:
8:REPAIRED after regress/artifacts/armmsrmodekill/PROBEATTACK_grok_20260917.txt (the attack on the
9:never-run first draft) -- see the `REPAIR' notes inline.  Summary of the repairs:
10:  R1  dump parsing: aligned base + little-endian assembly (read_mem32() in arm_bdt_probe.py,
11:      sw() in arm_flags_probe.py).  The first draft already carried both; kept.
12:  R2  EARLY/LATE SPLIT.  Every MSR session dumps the 0x9000 line TWICE (the arming dump of DEST
13:      before the stimulus, the result dump after it).  A first-match parse returns the EARLY
14:      line, where every post-MSR slot is still POISON -- so a correct fix would have read
15:      `nofire' on every kill row.  An `@MARK' pseudo-command becomes `print 0x5eed5eed' and
16:      the transcript is split at that token; arming is parsed only from before it, results
17:      only from after it.
18:  R3  `save 2s' plant and classifier agree, on the spec's own slots: return CPSR at DEST+8,
19:      SP at DEST+12, both inside the one dumped line.  The first draft planted SP at DEST+16
20:      and never dumped 0x9010, so ` sp' could never appear -- the row was ALWAYS red.  `rt'
21:      requires mode == 0x13 at the return slot, not mere existence.
22:  R4  the plant-dump of the MSR slot is SCORED: every MSR session dumps its whole planted
23:      stream before the stimulus and checks each word against WORDS, plus DEST == 0xd3 (the
24:      spec's "every later session repeats DEST==0xd3 + plant-dump").  A failure renders the
25:      row `unarmed', never `dead'.  This is what separates "died at the MSR" from "the MSR was
26:      never the instruction that ran".
27:  R5  CONTROL=DEAD stops the probe: `enc ok' red stops before any guest session; `live' or
28:      `pc adv' red stops before `armed'; `armed' red stops before any kill row.
29:  R6  `enc ok' note quoted the removed (w & 0x0FB0F000) mask; it now states the field-nibble
30:      test the code performs.  f_14 additionally checks rot == 0.
31:  R7  liveness: EOF on the pty is recorded; on EOF the child is reaped with a long deadline,
32:      without EOF with a short one (a live emulator never exits, and every live session used to
33:      burn the full 12 s).  The SIGKILL tail now READS THE STATUS: if waitpid shows the child
34:      exited on its own (not by our SIGKILL), alive is False.
35:  R8  canary accept rows also check arrival SP == 0 (spec: "arrive m=XX SP=0"), and `acc usr'
36:      now passes sp_at so a Load-skip (SP still BOOT_SP in USR32) reds it.
37:
38:THE DEFECT, verified by reading cpu_arm.c at HEAD ef577140 -- PRE-#562; #562 replaced both exits
39:with latched backstops, so these lines describe the unfixed tree only:
40:
41:    cpu_arm.c:606-608   arm_load_register_bank: default: fatal("...unimplemented mode %i"); exit(1);
42:    cpu_arm.c:559-561   arm_save_register_bank: default: same
43:
44:`0xE321F014' is `MSR CPSR_c, #0x14' -- mode 0x14 is a RESERVED ARM mode, so the Load arm's
45:`default:' is reached and the process dies.  `%i' prints DECIMAL: `unimplemented mode 20'.
46:
47:*** POLARITY: WANT IS POST-FIX CORRECT.  A PRE FAIL ON A DEFECT ROW *IS* THE REPRODUCTION. ***
48:*** ORACLE: EOF ALONE => DEAD.  THE TEXT IS DIAGNOSIS, NEVER HALF THE TRIGGER. ***
49:
50:#562 THE FIX AND WHAT THIS PROBE NOW DETECTS.  Three guest writers can put an unmodelled mode
51:(anything but 10 11 12 13 17 1b 1f) into CPSR, and each now DECLINES THE MODE FIELD ONLY, with a
52:`(once)' announce naming its site: msr_imm (`MSR CPSR_c'), arm_pop's `LDM {..pc}^' SPSR restore,
53:and the DPI S-to-PC SPSR restore (`MOVS pc,..', `SUBS pc,lr,..').  The restores keep the CURRENT
54:mode in M[4:0] and assign every other bit from the SPSR (DPI later forces T for an odd destination
55:PC; not driven here).  The Save/Load `default:' arms are BACKSTOPS (latched announce, return, no
56:exit(1)), reached only once an unmodelled mode is ALREADY in CPSR, which no guest instruction can
57:now install -- only a debugger `cpsr=' assignment.  After such a plant Save's default: is reached
58:by a guest `MSR CPSR_c' to a modelled mode (dbg save), a DPI S-to-PC (dbg both, latch rpt) or
59:exception entry; Load's default: ONLY by a DPI S-to-PC executed in the planted mode (dbg both,
60:latch rpt).  An `LDM {..pc}^' from a planted mode stops the CPU at arm_pop's selector default:
61:first (pre-existing; not this fix).  POST-FIX the guest is in SVC32 with the I/F bits the write
62:set -- `#0x14' clears I and F -- NOT in a reserved mode.  Rows added by #562: kill 1e, kill 03,
63:rst movs, rst ldm, zero spsr, acc movs, acc ldm, dbg save, dbg both, latch ind, latch rpt, src
64:dpi/src pop x {fiq irq abt und svc}, msr lbl, encl, tbit, encl2, msr wide, grid msr, grid dpi,
65:grid pop, grid cov, the `if=' (I/F) pin on
66:kill 14 / kill 15, and ` sp0' (an actual zero SP readback) on the rows whose SP is a never-loaded
67:bank.
68:
69:MODES 0x00-0x0F ARE NOW CLAIMED.  This header used to BAN `MSR CPSR_c, #0' as "the 26-bit hole,
70:a different defect".  The helper declines 0x00-0x0F like any other unmodelled value, and
71:`zero spsr' drives exactly mode 0x00 (an SPSR never written is zero: cpu_new zero-fills).
72:
73:THE GENERATED GRID (repair 5; owner ruling 2026-10-08).  The restore/MSR coverage is GENERATED
74:from tables (grid_obs(): labels, MODELLED, UNMODELLED, complementary value pairs), not written row
75:by row: `grid msr', `grid dpi', `grid pop' run every generated observation and compare the WHOLE
76:CPSR word; `grid cov' re-derives the G1 table (outcome x bit x polarity, aggregated over labels and
77:latch states) from the same generator and reds on any uncovered G1 cell.  G2, G3 and G4 hold by the
78:generator's construction (counted statically on the final pass: G2 80 of 80 label x bit cells, G3
79:96 of 96, G4 8 of 8), NOT by a row -- `grid cov' does not assert them.
80:  G1 every (path, outcome, bit 0..31, polarity) cell has an observation whose result bit DIFFERS
81:     from the wrong source -- OLD's bit for every non-mode bit and for an accept's mode bits; NEW's
82:     (the SPSR / operand's) bit for a DECLINE's mode bits, which must equal the LABEL.  Complementary
83:     pairs: p1 OLD = label (bits 31:5 clear) / NEW = 0xffffffe0 | mode (31:5 set, T SET); p2 OLD =
84:     0xffffffc0 | label (31:6 set, T clear) / NEW = mode (31:5 clear) -- so keep-old, force-0 and
85:     force-1 all change the word.  This is a UNION across observations, not a property of every
86:     decline.  (Repair 5's text said the result "must equal the SPSR / operand value while the OLD
87:     CPSR's bit differs (OLD 0 / NEW all-ones-with-T, and OLD all-ones / NEW 0)": FALSE for a
88:     decline's mode bits and for both pairs' OLD values; corrected 2026-10-09 from grok's and
89:     codex's final-pass readings, against grid_obs() and grid_cov().)
90:     Named equivalents: bit 4 polarity 0 and bit 4 on accept (every modelled mode and label
91:     has bit 4 set, so keep-old / force-1 equal the right answer there), and T
92:     polarity 0 against OLD T = 1 (the guest runs ARM code, so OLD T is always 0; keep-old T is
93:     caught at polarity 1).  The latch is SET for every decline after a session's first.
94:  G2 every msr_imm label (FIQ IRQ SVC ABT UND SYS) declines label ^ 0x1f, which differs in all
95:     five mode bits; the restore labels decline the same value as the SPSR.
96:  G3 all 25 unmodelled values are declined and all 7 modelled modes accepted on EACH path.
97:  G4 arm_pop's enclosing cells {S, non-S} x {PC, no PC}, all four, in grid pop.
98:  The hand-written rows below remain (G5): label x latch x outcome (src), tbit (T with the latch
99:  clear, by `print cpsr'), encl / encl2 (the DPI enclosing cells), msr wide, msr lbl.  Sessions:
100:  the probe prints ARMMSRMODE_SESSIONS.
101:
